  "title": "Rubric-Based Evaluation for Real World AI Systems",
  "description": "AI teams need to prove their systems behave responsibly, but turning policies, safety requirements, or product expectations into evaluations is still slow and manual. This talk introduces a way to translate natural-language requirements into testable artifacts: concrete behaviors, targeted test cases, evaluation runs, and evidence of where the system aligns or fails. It helps teams move from “we have a requirement” to “we can measure whether the system follows it.\n\nSeating for this session is first-come, first-served. Add it to your schedule to plan your day and arrive early to secure a spot.",
